@startuml persistent-lifecycle
' ============================================================================
' Persistent ARTrie file lifecycle — create → serve → checkpoint → close →
' reopen/recover, including the crash path. Source of truth:
' src/persistent_artrie/{mmap_ctor,io_uring_ctor}.rs (create/open),
' core/overlay/{durable_write,checkpoint}.rs, core/recovery.rs.
' Color key:  green = in-memory serving   blue = durable on-disk action
'             amber = recovery   red = crash
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
}

title Persistent ARTrie — file lifecycle

[*] --> Created : create(path)\n(fresh WAL + empty overlay)

Created --> Serving
state Serving #C8E6C9 {
  [*] --> Ready
  Ready --> Ready : get / contains\n(lock-free overlay read)
  Ready --> Ready : insert / upsert / remove\n(Order-A: WAL append+fsync → root CAS)
}

Serving --> Checkpointed : checkpoint()
state Checkpointed #BBDEFB : dense CX image written;\nWAL truncated to the\ncommitted watermark
Checkpointed --> Serving : resume

Serving --> Closed : drop / close (clean)
state Closed #ECEFF1
Serving --> Crashed : power loss / kill
state Crashed #FFCDD2

Closed --> Recovering : reopen(path)
Crashed --> Recovering : reopen(path)
state Recovering #FFE0B2 : load checkpoint image,\nthen replay durable WAL tail\n(LSN ≥ checkpoint_lsn)
Recovering --> Serving : acknowledged writes restored\n(un-acked writes were never durable)

legend right
| Color | Phase |
|<#C8E6C9>| in-memory serving |
|<#BBDEFB>| durable on-disk action |
|<#FFE0B2>| recovery |
|<#FFCDD2>| crash |
endlegend
@enduml
